{"seq":31,"trial_id":"gbrain-memory-2026-10/openclaw-haiku-gbrain-told-live-mu-memory/ms-05-vantorre-tickets/r4","wall_ts":"2026-10-27T02:22:26.918Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-16T09:00:00-05:00","args_digest":"080de982bfe5eeb74c094f13a31c28c1b3ee5af67ce8edcdffcf91a2f18d079e","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","text":"Nadia, here's what I found for Vantorre Group (the parent, not Mobility). I read #strategic-pod, #inc-vtg-hartford, and the team-strategic digests. Ticket numbers are reported as written in each source, and I haven't checked them against the ticket system.\n\n**Tickets and incident IDs**\n\n1. **#8841** (support, Allentown kiosk issue)\n   - Source: #strategic-pod, 2026-07-01 09:17 (ts 1782915420.000100). Gideon says he closed it with support after the browser-cache fix on the kiosk tablets.\n2. **INC-4821** (Hartford gate kiosk outage, 2026-08-03)\n   - Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, 2026-08-03 11:08 (ts 1785773280.000111). Gideon left it open for another arrival cycle, with a status-page access screenshot attached.\n3. **VT-55120** (root-cause ticket for the Hartford kiosk outage)\n   - Source: #inc-vtg-hartford, 2026-10-14 09:00 (ts 1791986400.000123). Carrowmere's gateway route finding and reconnect log are attached there.\n4. **#PD-8841** (missed carrier check-ins, Allentown Gate 4, 2nd shift)\n   - Source: teams/team-strategic/digests/2026-04-27-strategic-digest.md\n5. **#8841** (gate kiosk timeout, Allentown Dock Door 12, 2nd shift, still open)\n   - Source: teams/team-strategic/digests/2026-05-04-strategic-digest.md\n6. **#8841** (Newark Dock Door 14 check-in kiosk, escalated to platform engineering)\n   - Source: teams/team-strategic/digests/2026-09-30-strategic-digest.md\n7. **#PD-4418** (Carrier_Dwell_Summary export dropping timestamps on Door 9)\n   - Source: teams/team-strategic/digests/2025-09-15-strategic-digest.md. The digest says only \"the account Nadia runs,\" so I'm attributing it to Vantorre Group by inference.\n\n**Items with no ticket number** (in case you want them in the history)\n- 2025-03-10 digest: Mateo's email about gate check-in delays at Allentown.\n- 2026-05-03 digest: duplicate arrival entries at Door 14, and Mateo's export question.\n- 2026-08-03 digest: the Hartford Sev 1 incident. It doesn't name a ticket, but it's probably the same event as INC-4821.\n\n**Things to check before the steering committee**\n- **#8841 conflicts across sources.** It appears as #PD-8841 in April, then as an open Allentown kiosk ticket in May, closed in July in the pod channel, and as a new Newark ticket submitted by Mateo on 9/30. These descriptions may not all be the same ticket, so please confirm in the ticket system.\n- **Account ownership is inconsistent.** The Hartford channel and the digests don't agree on which of Gideon's or your accounts the industrial and Mobility items belong to, so the attribution above should be confirmed.\n\nI used the channel history, the digests and the brain, not a workspace-wide search. I haven't looked at the accounts/vantorre-group ticket folders. I can check those too if you want a fuller history."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"C36LMHRLAXI","ts":"1792159200.000126"}}
